[
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "defaultValue": "HA Watch"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "defaultValue": "Three lines of the watch face are yours: the line above the time and the two lines below it. Each takes up to two Home Assistant values. Leave a line empty and it keeps its default. Date, time and battery level are fixed and need no setup."
  },
  {
    "type": "section",
    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "defaultValue": "Connection"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "defaultValue": "The address must be reachable from your phone &mdash; so use the external URL, not <code>homeassistant.local</code>. Create the token in Home Assistant under <em>Profile &rarr; Security &rarr; Long-lived access tokens</em>."
      },
      {
        "type": "input",
        "messageKey": "haUrl",
        "label": "URL",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "attributes": {
          "placeholder": "https://ha.example.org",
          "type": "url",
          "autocorrect": "off",
          "autocapitalize": "off"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "input",
        "messageKey": "haToken",
        "label": "Access Token",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "attributes": {
          "placeholder": "eyJhbGciOi...",
          "autocorrect": "off",
          "autocapitalize": "off"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "section",
    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "defaultValue": "Line above the time"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "defaultValue": "Default: sunrise and sunset. You can find the entity ID in Home Assistant under <em>Settings &rarr; Devices &amp; Services &rarr; Entities</em>. If you leave the unit empty, the one from Home Assistant will be used. With only one entity the value uses the full width and the divider disappears."
      },
      {
        "type": "input",
        "messageKey": "entity3",
        "label": "Left Entity ID",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "attributes": {
          "placeholder": "sensor.outside_temperature",
          "autocorrect": "off",
          "autocapitalize": "off"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "input",
        "messageKey": "unit3",
        "label": "Left Unit",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "attributes": {
          "placeholder": "auto",
          "autocorrect": "off",
          "autocapitalize": "off"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "input",
        "messageKey": "entity4",
        "label": "Right Entity ID",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "attributes": {
          "placeholder": "sensor.humidity",
          "autocorrect": "off",
          "autocapitalize": "off"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "input",
        "messageKey": "unit4",
        "label": "Right Unit",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "attributes": {
          "placeholder": "auto",
          "autocorrect": "off",
          "autocapitalize": "off"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "section",
    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "defaultValue": "First line below the time"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "defaultValue": "Default: current weather, for example &ldquo;Clear, 14 &deg;C&rdquo;. This is the line that held your two values in version 1.1, so anything you set up there is still here."
      },
      {
        "type": "input",
        "messageKey": "entity1",
        "label": "Left Entity ID",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "attributes": {
          "placeholder": "sensor.storage_charge_level_total",
          "autocorrect": "off",
          "autocapitalize": "off"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "input",
        "messageKey": "unit1",
        "label": "Left Unit",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "attributes": {
          "placeholder": "auto",
          "autocorrect": "off",
          "autocapitalize": "off"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "input",
        "messageKey": "entity2",
        "label": "Right Entity ID",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "attributes": {
          "placeholder": "sensor.storage_available_energy",
          "autocorrect": "off",
          "autocapitalize": "off"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "input",
        "messageKey": "unit2",
        "label": "Right Unit",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "attributes": {
          "placeholder": "auto",
          "autocorrect": "off",
          "autocapitalize": "off"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "section",
    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "defaultValue": "Second line below the time"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "defaultValue": "Default: steps and distance, both read from the watch itself."
      },
      {
        "type": "input",
        "messageKey": "entity5",
        "label": "Left Entity ID",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "attributes": {
          "placeholder": "sensor.pv_power",
          "autocorrect": "off",
          "autocapitalize": "off"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "input",
        "messageKey": "unit5",
        "label": "Left Unit",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "attributes": {
          "placeholder": "auto",
          "autocorrect": "off",
          "autocapitalize": "off"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "input",
        "messageKey": "entity6",
        "label": "Right Entity ID",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "attributes": {
          "placeholder": "sensor.grid_power",
          "autocorrect": "off",
          "autocapitalize": "off"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "input",
        "messageKey": "unit6",
        "label": "Right Unit",
        "defaultValue": "",
        "attributes": {
          "placeholder": "auto",
          "autocorrect": "off",
          "autocapitalize": "off"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "section",
    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "defaultValue": "Time and Date"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "defaultValue": "&ldquo;Follow the watch&rdquo; uses the 24-hour setting from the watch itself, under <em>Settings &rarr; Date &amp; Time</em>. In 12-hour format a small &ldquo;am&rdquo; or &ldquo;pm&rdquo; sits to the left of the time. Sunrise and sunset only drop the leading zero &mdash; there is no room for a suffix next to the icons, and the icons already tell you which half of the day it is."
      },
      {
        "type": "select",
        "messageKey": "timeFormat",
        "label": "Format",
        "defaultValue": "watch",
        "options": [
          {
            "label": "Follow the watch",
            "value": "watch"
          },
          {
            "label": "24 hours",
            "value": "24"
          },
          {
            "label": "12 hours (am/pm)",
            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "defaultValue": "Weekday and month names are always English. &ldquo;Automatic&rdquo; puts the month first only in regions that write it that way, and the day first everywhere else."
      },
      {
        "type": "select",
        "messageKey": "dateFormat",
        "label": "Date",
        "defaultValue": "auto",
        "options": [
          {
            "label": "Automatic",
            "value": "auto"
          },
          {
            "label": "Tue, 25 Aug",
            "value": "dayMonth"
          },
          {
            "label": "Tue, Aug 25",
            "value": "monthDay"
          },
          {
            "label": "Tue, 25.08.",
            "value": "numericDe"
          },
          {
            "label": "Tue, 08/25",
            "value": "numericUs"
          },
          {
            "label": "2026-08-25",
            "value": "iso"
          },
          {
            "label": "Tu, 25. Aug (as before)",
            "value": "classic"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "section",
    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "defaultValue": "Weather"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "defaultValue": "Only used for the default of the first line below the time. Data comes from <a href=\"https://open-meteo.com\">Open-Meteo</a> for your current location; no account needed. There is no way to read the unit setting of the Pebble app, so &ldquo;Automatic&rdquo; goes by your phone's region &mdash; switch it here if that guesses wrong."
      },
      {
        "type": "select",
        "messageKey": "tempUnit",
        "label": "Temperature",
        "defaultValue": "auto",
        "options": [
          {
            "label": "Automatic",
            "value": "auto"
          },
          {
            "label": "Celsius (°C)",
            "value": "celsius"
          },
          {
            "label": "Fahrenheit (°F)",
            "value": "fahrenheit"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "submit",
    "defaultValue": "Save"
  }
]
